& [Selection]
  + preserve the official Codex public environment vocabulary and the exact inherited-environment behavior of Cantor's existing Phase3A observation runner as candidate inputs for B1 gap G03
  + this inventory does not select a Codex executable and does not authorize schema generation process launch environment-value inspection credential access authentication provider contact or observation receipt

& [OfficialCodexEnvironmentVocabulary]
  + [page] https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/environment-variables is the official Codex environment-variable page captured on 2026-08-23
  + the page identifies CODEX_HOME for CLI IDE app-server and installer state including configuration authentication logs sessions skills and packages
  + the page identifies CODEX_SQLITE_HOME for CLI and app-server SQLite state with configuration precedence over the variable
  + installer-only controls are CODEX_NON_INTERACTIVE and CODEX_INSTALL_DIR
  + noninteractive credential and trusted-automation inputs are CODEX_API_KEY and CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN
  + workload-identity inputs are OPENAI_FEDERATION_RULE_ID OPENAI_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE and OPENAI_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_CONTEXT
  + trust-store inputs are CODEX_CA_CERTIFICATE and fallback SSL_CERT_FILE
  + RUST_LOG controls CLI and app-server logging verbosity
  + the official page is a stable public vocabulary and not proof that these are the only ambient values read by the operating system dependencies subprocesses or either exact local binary

& [OfficialRustProcessSemantics]
  + [page] https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/process/struct.Command.html is the official Rust standard-library Command documentation captured on 2026-08-23
  + a Command child inherits the parent process environment by default
  + env_remove excludes one named variable while env_clear excludes all inherited variables before explicit additions
  + Windows variable names are case-insensitive and case-preserving so B1 comparison and denial must normalize names without assuming case distinguishes authority

& [ExactCurrentCantorRunner]
  + crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/workspace_admission/process.rs is 6102 bytes SHA256 1110C572F82E3A65F8EE71678276CE7FB13116ABCAD57A73ECCAC3E819E104D2 at repository commit 2783826c042c60f6b6a3fc45c7f66472f04f3ec6
  + the runner rehashes the pinned Git executable immediately before spawn and invokes the validated absolute executable path
  + it removes GIT_DIR GIT_WORK_TREE GIT_INDEX_FILE GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY GIT_COMMON_DIR GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES GIT_CONFIG and GIT_CONFIG_COUNT
  + it sets GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT to 0 GCM_INTERACTIVE to Never GIT_PAGER to cat and PAGER to cat
  + it does not call env_clear and therefore inherits every ambient variable not among the eight exact removals
  + this includes possible credential proxy trust state-root path shell Git-hook editor pager helper and diagnostic influences outside the current eight-name removal set
  + the Phase3A runner is useful predecessor evidence for executable hashing bounded streams deadlines and interruption but is not a safe environment template for B1

& [B1CandidateEnvironmentGrammar]
  + start from env_clear rather than attempting an open-ended blacklist against the ambient user process
  + compare Windows names case-insensitively and serialize the admitted name set in one canonical sorted spelling
  + invoke only an explicitly selected and rehashed absolute executable path so PATH and PATHEXT are not selection inputs
  + set CODEX_HOME and CODEX_SQLITE_HOME only to separately admitted disposable absolute roots whose pre-state post-state cleanup owner and recovery behavior are bound by G06
  + deny CODEX_API_KEY CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN OPENAI_FEDERATION_RULE_ID OPENAI_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE and OPENAI_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_CONTEXT for the provider-free schema and initialization probe
  + deny CODEX_CA_CERTIFICATE SSL_CERT_FILE HTTP_PROXY HTTPS_PROXY ALL_PROXY NO_PROXY and case variants unless a later source separately proves a required local-only exception
  + deny CODEX_NON_INTERACTIVE CODEX_INSTALL_DIR ambient PATH shell Git credential hook editor pager replacement-object and network-helper controls unless one exact nonsecret value is separately justified and admitted
  + admit only the minimal nonsecret operating-system process values proven necessary for the selected executable and fixed RUST_LOG behavior if it is required
  + bind admitted values by name and SHA256 digest while keeping raw values out of evidence narrative logs and protocol payloads
  + treat any extra observed name missing name value-digest drift state-root drift or executable drift as refusal before initialization

& [Delineation]
  + the official page closes the public Codex variable-name inventory but not the selected binary's complete runtime dependency set
  + the existing Phase3A runner proves partial Git hardening but also proves inherited ambient state remains available because env_clear is absent
  + an env_clear-first grammar is the smallest defensible B1 candidate and cannot become canonical until the selected executable survives it inside admitted disposable roots
  + no raw environment value variable enumeration user state authentication material or secret file was read for this source

& [GapDelta]
  + G03 changes from unspecified environment grammar to an official public Codex vocabulary one exact unsafe predecessor behavior and one bounded env_clear-first candidate grammar
  + G03 remains unresolved for the exact minimal operating-system allowlist selected-binary success refusal behavior and canonical name-value-digest serialization
  + G06 is narrowed by the official CODEX_HOME and CODEX_SQLITE_HOME state-root controls but remains unresolved for exact disposable roots pre-state cleanup recovery and owner
  + G01 G02 G04 G05 and G07 are unchanged

